From caeae3d4532d19ce777cced807e9460c650a894c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:23:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: restore the two-body player lost in the #15 merge
 resolution
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 'Merge main into feature/ballz-finished' conflict resolution took the
#13 side of ballz-play.ts and ballz-level-scene.ts, dropping the steer
control layer (keyboard aim/thrust + mouse point-and-launch), the caged
ball + fire-arrow entities, the steering block, the fog envelope, and the
nbrTour=3 lap honoring — while the runtime/host/rules halves survived,
leaving main internally inconsistent (smoke-ballz red). This restores the
feature branch's final versions; nothing from #13 is lost (its wood floor
and values are identical, its global-cap steering is superseded by the
per-axis legacy path plus the steer scheme). smoke-ballz green.
---
